  "id": "DrugBank_DB09350 - MONDO_3482",
  "verbalization": "Piperonyl Butoxide is implicated in the treatment of Pediculus humanus corporis infestation through a chain of indications involving pyrethrum extract. The drug is linked to both Pthirus pubis infestation and Pediculus humanus capitis infestation, both of which are caused by the same parasite, Pediculus humanus. This suggests a potential shared mechanism of action or pharmacological interaction between Piperonyl Butoxide and pyrethrum extract, which is known to target the nervous system of mites. The evidence from the two paths indicates that Piperonyl Butoxide may act as a mediator in the treatment of infestations, possibly by enhancing the effects of pyrethrum extract. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Piperonyl Butoxide in the management of scabies-like infestations, though further research is needed to confirm its direct therapeutic effect on Pediculus humanus corporis.",
